# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: windows-runner-sunset-probe-campaign — write & run the probes that only AutoCAD can answer, before the Windows runner is lost
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: campaign

* Deadline and why it bites

The Windows CI runner is expected to go away in *8 weeks* (filed 2026-10-24,
so target *~2026-12-19*). It is the fleet's ONLY path to real AutoCAD:
AutoCAD runs on Windows alone, and the vendor probe jobs reach it through
=accoreconsole.exe= on that runner. BricsCAD, by contrast, also runs natively
on macOS (thalassa) year-round, so BricsCAD answers are NOT on the clock.

Therefore the scarce, perishable resource is *AutoCAD ground truth*. Every
spec entry whose only authority is a real AutoCAD — a divergence from
BricsCAD, an AutoCAD-Windows-only function, a prompt sequence clautolisp's
=(command ...)= depends on — becomes unverifiable the day the runner stops.
This campaign front-loads exactly those.

This is the sunset-scoped successor to =cad-vendor-probe-campaign= (P1, closed
2026-10-03, which drove the first probe suites onto CI) and the execution arm
of =deferred-spec-research.issue= and the =autolisp-spec= PLAN's "run the
probes on a real AutoCAD" line (open since 2026-04-26, blocked then on a
license seat).

* Method (unchanged from the existing probe machinery)

Evidence ranking (specification-resolution-plan.org): vendor docs < executable
product tests. The probes ARE the product tests, and this file is the plan for
writing the ones still missing.

How a probe reaches AutoCAD, concretely:

- The vendor-neutral suite lives in =probes/sources/probe-*.lsp= + one line in
  =probes/sources/manifest.txt=. No Makefile/shell/YAML change is needed to
  add a suite (probes/README.org § Adding a probe suite).
- =scripts/ci-detect-probe-changes.py= maps =probes/**= to the =suite= family,
  so any new suite makes =PROBES_CHANGED =~ /,suite,/= and the existing jobs
  =probe:suite:autocad:windows= and =probe:suite:bricscad:{windows,macos}=
  run it automatically on the MR that adds it. Those jobs are otherwise
  *manual* (=when: manual, allow_failure: true=), i.e. playable by hand
  whenever the intermittent runner is up — which is the "launched manually
  when the windows CI runners are available" the campaign asks for.
- Results commit to =probe-results/<product>/<platform>/<timestamp>/= (locally)
  or travel as a 90-day artefact (in CI, =PROBE_NO_COMMIT=). The sexp records
  are then folded into the spec entry's "Tested Behaviour" subsection and the
  matching =;;; SPEC-UNCERTAIN:= / =;;; Vendor:= marker in the source.

Portability rules that every suite here obeys (probes/README.org):

- A form a host might refuse to PARSE or evaluate is held as a STRING and
  =(eval (read text))='d at run time, so a refusal is that one case's recorded
  =error=, never a dead LOAD or a dead run. Case name == exact expression.
- No =(setq x (or x d))= (BricsCAD =or= returns T/nil). Emit only through the
  =cad-probe-*= helpers.

Two hazards that keep specific probes OUT of the normal suite:

1. *Uncatchable aborts.* BricsCAD V26 *aborts the application* on real
   =(/ 1.0 0.0)= (spec ch.8 harvest). =vl-catch-all-apply= cannot catch an
   app abort, so such a case would take the whole BricsCAD run down — the same
   hazard =probe-load-refusal.lsp= is quarantined for. Divide-by-zero and
   kin go in a QUARANTINED suite (run alone + split, low timeout,
   PROBE_ANY_RESULT_IS_SUCCESS) or are made AutoCAD-only. See batch B13.
2. *Headless ceiling.* =accoreconsole= has no UI, no ActiveX, no viewport DCS,
   and may not load Express Tools. So reactor firing, =vlax-for= over a live
   collection, interactive command prompts, and the Arbitrary-Axis UCS-matrix
   question cannot be fully answered headless. Those batches (B10–B12) must
   either prove they work under accoreconsole FIRST (one gating probe) or be
   scheduled on a GUI AutoCAD session — the harder, scarcer slot, so they rank
   high on the calendar even when individual value is mixed.

* Prioritisation principle

Rank by *perishability first, value second*: AutoCAD-only-answerable >
both-vendor-divergence (AutoCAD half perishable) > BricsCAD-only or
both-confirm (not perishable — do after sunset on macOS). Within a rank, a
correctness-critical gap (something clautolisp actively relies on, e.g. a
=(command ...)= prompt token, an ERRNO code, a sysvar read-only flag that makes
portable =setvar= error) beats a cosmetic one.

* Backlog, batched as probe suites

Each BATCH is one =probe-*.lsp= suite (unless marked otherwise) and runs under
=probe:suite:*:windows/macos=. "AC-crit" = the answer is lost at sunset.
Source: the 2026-10-24 spec harvest (4 readers over the 160k-line draft) +
the 18 =;;; SPEC-UNCERTAIN:= markers in
=clautolisp/autolisp-builtins-core/source/api.lisp= + =deferred-spec-research=.

** B1 — numeric-edges  [LANDED this MR]  AC-crit: YES
probe-numeric-edges.lsp. Integer width/overflow (does AutoCAD wrap / promote /
signal at >=2^31? clautolisp SIGNALS), negative integer division rounding
(=/ -7 2= -> -3 vs -4; REM sign), atoi/atof lexical edges (AutoCAD halves:
octal-on-0, 0x autodetect, C99 hex-float =0x1p4=, locale comma, leading space,
trailing junk). Baseline already shows a clautolisp-vs-BricsCAD divergence:
=(atof "0x1p4")= is 0.0 on clautolisp, 16.0 on BricsCAD V26 — AutoCAD unknown.

** B2 — vle (BricsCAD Visual Lisp Extensions)  [LANDED this MR]  AC-crit: NO
probe-vle.lsp. Retires 9 =SPEC-UNCERTAIN= markers at once: vle-subst-nth
out-of-range IDX, vle-list-split result shape, vle-member boolean-vs-tail,
vle-vector-normalise zero-length, vle-vector-getucs +-Z orientation,
vle-string-replace first-vs-all, vle-string-split empty tokens, vle-aci2rgb
10–249 range, vle-rgb2aci arg shape. Behaviour is BricsCAD's (answerable on
macOS); the AutoCAD column confirms absence for each symbol's Availability line.

** B3 — reader-printer  AC-crit: YES (reader/printer authority perishes)
probe-reader-printer.lsp (all string+read, safe). From ch.2/12/13/14 harvest:
read trailing/between-call comment handling (=(read "1 ; two")=,
=(read "1 ;| c |; 2")=); real-literal reader (=.5=, =1.=, =1.e6=, =+.5=,
=1E+03= — and that =1.= reads as 1.0, not CL integer 1); symbol-token grammar
(=a#b=, =a[b]=, =a:b=, =|a b|=, =a.b=); string-literal escape repertoire
(=\101= octal, =\x41=, =\uNNNN=, unknown escape =\q=); prin1 escape repertoire
on control chars / embedded quote+backslash / non-ASCII / astral (build the
input with =chr= at run time, record the round-trip form). Critical for
reader/printer round-trip portability.

** B4 — setvar-edges  AC-crit: YES
probe-setvar-edges.lsp (getvar/setvar with save+restore). Highest ch.16 value:
the spec's integer-range rule is internally CONTRADICTORY (clamp to
[-32768,32767] vs signal) — =(setvar "OSMODE" 70000)= then read back, or an
error+ERRNO? Also setvar type-coercion strictness (=(setvar "CMDECHO" 1.0)=
error or coerce?), setvar on unknown/read-only name (error form + ERRNO),
ANGBASE/SNAPANG radians-regardless-of-AUNITS. Measure on both; AutoCAD half
perishes.

** B5 — sysvar read-only & default sweep  AC-crit: YES
probe-sysvar-flags.lsp (extends the harvest:sysvars mechanism). The spec
carries hundreds of per-vendor Divergence rows for read-only flags and default
values, harvested from docs, never measured. SECURELOAD is self-contradictory
(entry "read-only yes" vs its Divergence row "AutoCAD False, BricsCAD True") —
security-critical (gates load/arxload). Confirm read-only on AutoCAD for
BACKZ/FRONTZ (claimed RO on AutoCAD) and writability of TRUSTEDPATHS /
LENSLENGTH / PUCSBASE / LEGACYCODESEARCH. Batch-sweep the default-value
Divergence set (DIMZIN, APERTURE, …) on a clean imperial template — a one-shot
=getvar= over the divergent-name list, AutoCAD defaults unverifiable after
sunset. (The ~300 "AutoCAD Integer / BricsCAD Short" type rows are NOT
probe-worthy — representation, already consistent.)

** B6 — load & encoding  AC-crit: YES  (needs byte-inspection, see note)
probe-load-encoding.lsp + a small file round-trip harness. load missing-file
error form + ERRNO + onfailure handling ("host- and version-sensitive"); load
of BOM-less UTF-8 vs UTF-8+BOM vs UTF-16LE source on AutoCAD (code-point
compare); OPEN "a"/"w"/"r" with "utf8-bom" — does a CREATE write a leading BOM,
does a READ skip it or return U+FEFF, behaviour at LISPSYS 0. Needs leading-byte
inspection of the written file (EF BB BF), which the current sexp harness does
not do — add a tiny read-raw-bytes helper or a companion .ps1 step. Overlaps the
existing encoding:experiment jobs; reuse that harness where possible.

** B7 — arx / vba (AutoCAD-Windows ONLY)  AC-crit: YES
probe-arx-vba.lsp. No BricsCAD analogue at all, so sunset = never. arxload
double-load error + ERRNO; arxunload of a locked default module; =(arx)=
fresh-session module list + macOS .bundle/.crx forms; vl-vbaload missing-file
return/error; vl-vbarun bad-macro return. These touch the real host state —
keep each under vl-catch-all-apply and avoid side effects.

** B8 — host functions  AC-crit: mixed (do AutoCAD halves first)
probe-host-fns.lsp. snvalid char-rejection set under EXTNAMES 0/1 + bar flag;
cvunit (acad.unt contents, degC->degF offset, incompatible->nil); getenv/setenv
empty-vs-undefined + persistence + case; getcfg/setcfg invalid-name->nil +
512-char truncation; startapp return/PATH-search/quoting; menucmd unsupported
area on BricsCAD (error vs ignore); getcname localized<->English (needs a
localized AutoCAD — scarcest of all, flag separately); menugroup Windows-vs-
macOS return; tablet ERRNO with no digitiser.

** B9 — entity access / entmake / entmod / entget / ERRNO  AC-crit: YES
probe-entity-access.lsp (extends the entity-lifecycle scenario probes). ch.17
harvest: entmake R13+ subclass-marker rejection on AutoCAD (confirms the
normative rule; D1 already implemented, re-confirm the ERRNO=36); entget
default group-code set + header pair ORDER after entmake (flagged "not
normative"); entnext/entlast confinement of non-graphical XRECORD/DICTIONARY
(clautolisp enumerates them — divergence); entmod on a non-graphical object
(AutoCAD no-op vs BricsCAD applies — D3, re-confirm); ssget "X" malformed -4
operator tail (error/ERRNO vs silent partial match); ERRNO codes after failed
entmake/entmod/entnext-past-end. Several were measured in
vendor-probe-autocad-bricscad-divergences; capture the still-open ERRNO/order
details before sunset.

** B10 — Express Tools (ch.23 acet-*)  AC-crit: YES  (GATED)
probe-express-tools.lsp. FIRST a gating probe: =(acet-load-expresstools)= then
=(acet-str-equal "a" "a")= under accoreconsole — if Express Tools do not bind
headless, the whole chapter needs a GUI AutoCAD session (schedule accordingly).
If they bind: acet-str-find index base + not-found sentinel + regex;
acet-str-replace count/regex; acet-str-format printf directive set;
acet-str-wcmatch/equal/collate return types; acet-file-cwd/dir/mkdir formats;
acet-sys-lasterr/procid types. All "Vendor-defined" in the spec, AutoCAD-only.
(Dialog/pointer acet-ui-*, acad_colordlg are GUI — defer or drop.)

** B11 — ActiveX / reactors (ch.19/20/21)  AC-crit: YES  (GUI / live state)
probe-activex-reactors.lsp — likely NOT headless. vlax-map-collection aggregate
return (under-specified); vlax-for binds-vs-assigns loop var + survival;
reactor firing under accoreconsole + the accepted event-name vocabulary
(=:vlr-commandEnded= …). These need a live collection / a command to fire a
reactor; prove headless feasibility with one probe, else GUI session. BricsCAD
ActiveX parity items (vlax-tmatrix, vlr-* constructor set, vlr-pers family) are
NOT perishable — macOS/after-sunset.

** B12 — COMMAND prompt/option capture (the 85 cador-implemented commands)  AC-crit: YES  [HIGHEST LEVERAGE]
Not a probes/ suite — a dedicated prompt-capture harness
(scripts/run-command-prompts-probe.*) that drives each command one token at a
time under AutoCAD and logs the verbatim prompt strings + [bracketed] keyword
order. clautolisp's =(command ...)= feeds these token sequences, yet the
Options/Argument-Sequence rows in ch.28 are doc-harvested, never product-
captured. The implemented set (LINE, ARC, CIRCLE, TRIM, EXTEND, FILLET, OFFSET,
HATCH/-HATCH, INSERT/-INSERT, PEDIT, ARRAY→ARRAYRECT/PATH/POLAR, -LAYER,
-LINETYPE, MEASURE/DIVIDE, …) is the correctness-critical subset. AutoCAD's
prompts are the irreplaceable half (BricsCAD's stay capturable on macOS). Known
divergences to pin: TRIM/EXTEND Quick-vs-Standard mode (TRIMEXTENDMODE), bare
INSERT opening the Blocks palette vs classic -INSERT, OFFSET "Both Sides"
(BricsCAD-only), FILLET Expression/Chain/Loop. Also the command-PRESENCE
sweeps: the 706 "AutoCAD: not present" and the version-drift names
(3DPAN, EATTEXT, CLASSIC*, JOGSECTION/DETECT, ASSISTANTOPEN, MENULOAD) — batch-
type each, record "Unknown command" vs a prompt; any hit reclassifies the
portability row. This batch is the single best use of a live AutoCAD slot.

** B13 — divide-by-zero & abort hazards (QUARANTINED)  AC-crit: YES
probe-div-zero.lsp, manifest flag =quarantine=, run via PROBE_SUITES like
load-refusal (alone, split, low timeout, any-result-is-success). =(/ 1 0)=,
=(/ 1.0 0.0)=, =(/ 0.0 0.0)=, =(rem 1 0)=: trappable error vs value vs hard
abort, per vendor. MUST NOT be in the normal manifest (BricsCAD aborts).

* 8-week schedule (front-load the perishable + the GUI-scarce)

Weeks are elastic to the runner's office-hours availability; each batch is
one MR that auto-runs its suite on the next online window, then manual re-runs.

- *Week 1 (done in this MR):* B1 numeric-edges, B2 vle. Pattern + harness proven.
- *Week 1–2:* B3 reader-printer, B4 setvar-edges — pure value probes, highest
  AC-crit density, zero new harness.
- *Week 2–3:* B12 command prompt-capture harness + the implemented-set run.
  Start early: it is the highest-leverage AutoCAD-only work and needs a new
  driver (iterate against the runner while it is reliably up). Fold in the
  presence sweeps.
- *Week 3–4:* B9 entity/ERRNO, B5 sysvar read-only + default sweep.
- *Week 4–5:* B6 load/encoding (byte-inspection harness), B7 arx/vba.
- *Week 5–6:* B10 Express Tools (run the gating probe first; if GUI-only, book
  the GUI slot now), B8 host-fns (AutoCAD halves; getcname localized if a
  localized seat exists).
- *Week 6–7:* B11 ActiveX/reactors (headless-feasibility probe, else GUI slot).
  B13 quarantined div-zero (quick, any time a split run is scheduled).
- *Week 7–8:* buffer — re-run flaky/empty results, fold every captured
  results.sexp into the spec "Tested Behaviour" subsections and flip the
  =SPEC-UNCERTAIN= markers to =Vendor:= cites. The RESULTS are the deliverable;
  an unfolded result is half-done.

* Risks / limits

- *Intermittent runner:* a batch's job is manual; a maintainer plays it when
  the runner is online. Do not gate anything that must happen on a schedule on
  this runner (the release-1.8.43 lesson).
- *Headless ceiling:* B10–B12 may need a GUI AutoCAD; that slot is scarcer than
  the runner — book it deliberately, do not discover the need in week 8.
- *License seat:* full AutoCAD (vs accoreconsole) needs a seat; the
  autolisp-spec PLAN's AutoCAD run has been blocked on exactly this since
  2026-04-26. Confirm a seat is reachable on the Windows runner early.
- *Fold-back debt:* capturing is cheap; folding results into 974 spec entries +
  source markers is the real cost. Budget week 7–8 for it and keep each batch's
  spec edits in its own MR so nothing is left as a loose artefact.

* Status

NEXT. Harness proven and the first two suites (B1 numeric-edges, B2 vle) landed
in the MR that files this issue; they auto-run on =probe:suite:*:windows/macos=
on the next online window and are manually re-playable thereafter. B3–B13 are
specified above with exact probe expressions (from the 2026-10-24 spec harvest)
and a schedule. The 18 =SPEC-UNCERTAIN= markers and the open
=deferred-spec-research= questions are the fold-back targets.
